From: =?UTF-8?q?Berkay=20K=C3=B6sebay?= <brkosebay@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: composite: draw no extra Apple current while
 suspended

The extra current an Apple host grants must not be drawn while the bus
is suspended. reset_config() could apply it during suspend, because the
suspended flag was cleared only at the end of composite_resume(). Skip
the extra current while suspended and clear the flag before the
configuration is applied again on resume.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/usb/gadget/composite.c | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/composite.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/composite.c
index 1da3effb2..ea76d3918 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/composite.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/composite.c
@@ -959,7 +959,7 @@ static void reset_config(struct usb_composite_dev *cdev)
 static void composite_vbus_draw(struct usb_composite_dev *cdev, unsigned int mA)
 {
 	cdev->vbus_draw_ma = mA;
-	if (mA && cdev->apple_extra_ma)
+	if (mA && !cdev->suspended && cdev->apple_extra_ma)
 		mA = max(500 + cdev->apple_extra_ma, 0);
 	usb_gadget_vbus_draw(cdev->gadget, mA);
 }
@@ -2665,6 +2665,7 @@ void composite_resume(struct usb_gadget *gadget)
 	DBG(cdev, "resume\n");
 	if (cdev->driver->resume)
 		cdev->driver->resume(cdev);
+	cdev->suspended = 0;
 	if (cdev->config) {
 		list_for_each_entry(f, &cdev->config->functions, list) {
 			/*
@@ -2695,8 +2696,6 @@ void composite_resume(struct usb_gadget *gadget)
 		maxpower = min(maxpower, 100U);
 		composite_vbus_draw(cdev, maxpower);
 	}
-
-	cdev->suspended = 0;
 }
 
